\frametitle{Architecting for Resilience: Defending the EKF}
\begin{block}{The NaN Infection}
If an accelerometer glitches due to shock and sends an Attitude roll value of \texttt{NaN} (Not a Number), it infects the EKF matrix. Since mathematically $NaN \times 5 = NaN$, the entire covariance matrix becomes $NaN$ on the very first multiplication. The filter is permanently destroyed and cannot recover without a hard reboot.
\end{block}
\vspace{2mm}
\textbf{The Defense:}
We validate every incoming float using standard library macros before it is ever allowed to touch the math engine.
\begin{lstlisting}[style=cstyle]
#include <math.h>

if (isnan(att->roll) || isnan(att->pitch) || isnan(att->yaw)) {
    parser->packets_dropped++;
    return;  /* Reject the packet. EKF keeps its previous valid state. */
}
\end{lstlisting}
